<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Sentrachem interim shr plunges.</title>
<headline>Sentrachem interim shr plunges.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Feb 28</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     111.4 loss  vs 55.0 profit</p>
<p>    Pre-excep shr (cts)   24.4	  vs 55.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 10.0	  vs 14.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional item	327.0 loss  vs nil</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast Sentrachem's earnings for the six months ended February 28 sliding into loss, ranging between 60.0 and 80.0 cents a share with consensus at 68.3 cents.  </p>
<p>    Attrib income	   217.0 loss  vs 101.0 profit</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   257.0 loss  vs 113.0 profit</p>
<p>    Tax			 63.0 rebate vs 8.0 charge</p>
<p>    Net income		194.0 loss  vs 105.0 profit</p>
<p>    Net interest paid     99.0	  vs 70.0</p>
<p>    Turnover		  2,475.0     vs 2,323.0</p>
<p>Div payable May 12</p>
<p>on register April 25</p>
<p>Full name: Sentrachem Ltd</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
